<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Aug 27.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Aug 27.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF AUGUST 27 VERSUS AUGUST 20, 1996		 DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   11/22    0/11    252/221   85/941  348/348    187</p>
<p> SASK.	0/3     0/1	67/61    10/10    77/75	40</p>
<p> B.C.	 0/1     0/1	18/15    14/17    32/34	14</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/2	2/2	4/4	  0</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 2/1	0/1	2/2	  3</p>
<p> TOTAL     11/26    0/13    341/300  111/124  463/463    244</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>-- Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624</p>
